{"i":0,"start_s":0.08,"end_s":1.26,"speaker":"SPEAKER_00","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Mr. President"}
{"i":1,"start_s":2.03,"end_s":3.98,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":true,"text":"The Senator"}
{"i":2,"start_s":4.42,"end_s":5.52,"speaker":"SPEAKER_00","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"from Oregon"}
{"i":3,"start_s":5.97,"end_s":11.7,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Mr. President, climate disruption is a seminal challenge of our generation."}
{"i":4,"start_s":11.7,"end_s":21.75,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"It is the most significant test that human civilization on our planet has faced and there's a lot of questions about how we're going to be able to come"}
{"i":5,"start_s":22.16,"end_s":22.76,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"together as a"}
{"i":6,"start_s":22.76,"end_s":25.09,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"community of nations, community"}
{"i":7,"start_s":25.53,"end_s":25.54,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":true,"text":"of"}
{"i":8,"start_s":25.7,"end_s":25.71,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"of"}
{"i":9,"start_s":25.74,"end_s":35.78,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"cultures to address this very significant threat to our beautiful blue-green planet. It affects everything, from our farms, to our forests,"}
{"i":10,"start_s":35.78,"end_s":48.34,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"to our fisheries. We see the impact in terms of disappearing glaciers and shrinking ice sheets and melting permafrost and dying coral."}
{"i":11,"start_s":48.54,"end_s":53.7,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"And we see the impact on our farms and our trout streams and our forests."}
{"i":12,"start_s":53.68,"end_s":58.64,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"We see the impact with migrating animals, and migrating insects, and certainly more"}
{"i":13,"start_s":58.64,"end_s":81.2,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"powerful storms. In response, communities across the globe are taking action. They're transforming their energy economies. They're developing aggressive strategies to save energy in their buildings, and in their vehicles, and in their appliances. And they're working to replace their fossil fuel energy supplies"}
{"i":14,"start_s":81.46,"end_s":100.04,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"with renewable, clean and renewable energy. How much do you know about the changes underway? Let's find out. Welcome to Episode 3 of the Senate Climate Disruption Quiz. First question"}
{"i":15,"start_s":100.34,"end_s":101.2,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"we have: Why"}
{"i":16,"start_s":101.3,"end_s":101.91,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"did American"}
{"i":17,"start_s":101.91,"end_s":108.86,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Airlines cancel 57 flights between June 20th and 22nd? Was it extreme"}
{"i":18,"start_s":108.86,"end_s":110.49,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"temperatures?"}
{"i":19,"start_s":111.23,"end_s":119.97,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Was it a pilot strike? Was it severe storms? Was it a fuel shortage?"}
{"i":20,"start_s":120.45,"end_s":122.76,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"The"}
{"i":21,"start_s":123.83,"end_s":129.88,"speaker":"SPEAKER_07","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"answer"}
{"i":22,"start_s":129.88,"end_s":133.45,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"is A, extreme temperatures."}
{"i":23,"start_s":133.97,"end_s":134.53,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Well, how"}
{"i":24,"start_s":134.53,"end_s":136.9,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"is that the case?"}
{"i":25,"start_s":137.34,"end_s":137.64,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"When air"}
{"i":26,"start_s":137.68,"end_s":139.66,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"gets hotter, it gets"}
{"i":27,"start_s":139.66,"end_s":140.68,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"thinner,"}
{"i":28,"start_s":140.75,"end_s":140.76,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":true,"text":"and"}
{"i":29,"start_s":141.04,"end_s":149.04,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"thinner air provides less lift for planes to take off. And eventually the runway just isn't long enough for the"}
{"i":30,"start_s":149.22,"end_s":157.25,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"plane to go fast enough to get enough lift to clear the runway. And so, therefore, all of these flights get canceled."}
{"i":31,"start_s":157.36,"end_s":158.3,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"It's not the first"}
{"i":32,"start_s":158.34,"end_s":170.82,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"time it's happened. It happened in 2013 in Phoenix with 18 flights cancelled. But this was a pretty dramatic incident attributable to very extreme temperatures."}
{"i":33,"start_s":171,"end_s":171.99,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Let's turn"}
{"i":34,"start_s":171.99,"end_s":173.77,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"to question two."}
{"i":35,"start_s":173.8,"end_s":174.94,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"How long was"}
{"i":36,"start_s":175.08,"end_s":180.87,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"the recent streak of record-setting monthly temperatures? Meaning, for"}
{"i":37,"start_s":181.04,"end_s":184.44,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"example, that a given month like May was the hottest May ever."}
{"i":38,"start_s":184.64,"end_s":184.65,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":true,"text":"and"}
{"i":39,"start_s":184.66,"end_s":184.96,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"June"}
{"i":40,"start_s":184.96,"end_s":192.96,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"was the hottest June ever, and July was the hottest July ever. How many months in a row did this happen? Did it happen"}
{"i":41,"start_s":193.25,"end_s":194.69,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"for six months"}
{"i":42,"start_s":194.69,"end_s":195.75,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"in a row? Or"}
{"i":43,"start_s":195.76,"end_s":198.84,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"for 12 months in a row?"}
{"i":44,"start_s":198.84,"end_s":199.08,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Is it"}
{"i":45,"start_s":199.1,"end_s":207.41,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"conceivable that this streak extended beyond a year to 16 months? Or perhaps even for two years to 24"}
{"i":46,"start_s":207.42,"end_s":208.46,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"months?"}
{"i":47,"start_s":208.43,"end_s":209.48,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Lock in"}
{"i":48,"start_s":209.72,"end_s":211.87,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"your answers."}
{"i":49,"start_s":213.15,"end_s":217.99,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"The correct"}
{"i":50,"start_s":217.99,"end_s":226.91,"speaker":"SPEAKER_11","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"answer is C: 16 months. From May"}
{"i":51,"start_s":227.49,"end_s":236.62,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"2015 through August of 2016, each and every month was the hottest month on record."}
{"i":52,"start_s":236.61,"end_s":236.85,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":true,"text":"In"}
{"i":53,"start_s":237.16,"end_s":252.64,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"September 2016, the streak was broken, but only by a few hundredths of a degree. In fact, in September 2016, the temperature was still 1.6 degrees Fahrenheit above the 20th century average. Now,"}
{"i":54,"start_s":252.73,"end_s":252.74,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"I"}
{"i":55,"start_s":252.76,"end_s":266.25,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"have a little math question to put in here. If you had climate data, temperature data, for 50 years, what are the odds that by chance, 16 months in a row,"}
{"i":56,"start_s":266.51,"end_s":268.47,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"would be the hottest,"}
{"i":57,"start_s":268.69,"end_s":277.19,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"each one the hottest among the 50 previous months. What are the odds of that? Well, pull out your calculators"}
{"i":58,"start_s":277.19,"end_s":277.38,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"and"}
{"i":59,"start_s":277.39,"end_s":284.58,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"take one out of 50 and take it to the 16th power and what do"}
{"i":60,"start_s":284.82,"end_s":285.96,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"you get? You"}
{"i":61,"start_s":285.96,"end_s":295.02,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"get the odds are less than one out of a trillion trillion. That's the odds."}
{"i":62,"start_s":295.15,"end_s":295.37,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"In"}
{"i":63,"start_s":295.57,"end_s":295.94,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"other"}
{"i":64,"start_s":295.94,"end_s":299.19,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"words, this didn't happen by"}
{"i":65,"start_s":299.38,"end_s":302.65,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"chance."}
{"i":66,"start_s":302.99,"end_s":303.76,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Let's turn to"}
{"i":67,"start_s":304.56,"end_s":305.49,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"question number"}
{"i":68,"start_s":305.51,"end_s":316.92,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"three. Where in the world is the largest floating solar project? Maybe you've never even heard of a floating solar project, but there is one."}
{"i":69,"start_s":317.03,"end_s":317.47,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"In fact,"}
{"i":70,"start_s":317.47,"end_s":323.95,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"there are several. Where is the world's largest? Is it in China? Is it in Brazil?"}
{"i":71,"start_s":324.49,"end_s":324.5,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Is"}
{"i":72,"start_s":324.51,"end_s":330.78,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"it in India, or is it in Australia?"}
{"i":73,"start_s":330.91,"end_s":331.38,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"And by"}
{"i":74,"start_s":331.47,"end_s":340.45,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"the way, here is a hint, all four of these actually have floating solar projects. Lock in your answer."}
{"i":75,"start_s":341.01,"end_s":345.42,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"And here is the"}
