{"i":103,"start_s":522.29,"end_s":532.6,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"then you see the growth of companies like Tesla that only produces electric cars. And it is becoming increasingly clear that the future"}
{"i":104,"start_s":532.75,"end_s":532.97,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"of the"}
{"i":105,"start_s":533.02,"end_s":540.2,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"global auto industry is electric. Let's turn to question number five, our"}
{"i":106,"start_s":540.34,"end_s":541.82,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"final question. And"}
{"i":107,"start_s":541.83,"end_s":549.39,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"this one hits close to home for me as a senator from Oregon:"}
{"i":108,"start_s":549.39,"end_s":549.4,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"\"What killed"}
{"i":109,"start_s":549.63,"end_s":568.85,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"billions of baby oysters in Oregon in 2007 and 2008. Was it red tide? Red tide occurs when an algae blooms and it's a red bloom. It discolors the water, turns it red, and it releases"}
{"i":110,"start_s":569.25,"end_s":573.26,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"toxins that are absorbed by the clams and other sea life."}
{"i":111,"start_s":573.46,"end_s":573.47,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":true,"text":"We"}
{"i":112,"start_s":573.48,"end_s":580.35,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"can't go out and dig up our clams and eat them for fear of getting poisoned?"}
{"i":113,"start_s":580.57,"end_s":580.58,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Was"}
{"i":114,"start_s":580.58,"end_s":599.91,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"it red tide that killed the oysters? Or was it the POBS virus, the Pacific Oyster Mortality Syndrome, which affects Pacific oysters and can cause up to 100% mortality within days of initial detection? Was it sea lice, tiny jellyfish larvae that are tiny, almost invisible specks,"}
{"i":115,"start_s":599.91,"end_s":602.61,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"no larger than a grain of pepper?"}
{"i":116,"start_s":602.7,"end_s":602.86,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Or"}
{"i":117,"start_s":603.21,"end_s":608,"speaker":"SPEAKER_03","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"was it rising ocean acidity caused by the emission"}
{"i":118,"start_s":608,"end_s":618.24,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"of billions of tons of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases into the air and then absorbed by the ocean through tidal action?"}
{"i":119,"start_s":618.66,"end_s":626.2,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Lock in your answer. Music"}
{"i":120,"start_s":626.19,"end_s":630.11,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"The correct"}
{"i":121,"start_s":630.11,"end_s":639.21,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"answer is D, rising ocean acidity. How"}
{"i":122,"start_s":639.21,"end_s":640.05,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"is this"}
{"i":123,"start_s":640.05,"end_s":641.97,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"possible? How"}
{"i":124,"start_s":641.97,"end_s":642.65,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"can you"}
{"i":125,"start_s":642.65,"end_s":654.35,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"stand on the coast of Oregon and look out at the Pacific Ocean and envision that humankind has burned so much water?"}
{"i":126,"start_s":654.64,"end_s":678.2,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"fossil fuels, so many fossil fuels, so much that it has created so much carbon dioxide in the air and tidal action has absorbed that into the ocean and turned it into carbonic acid that it's changed the acidity of the ocean. It seems completely impossible. And yet, over the last 150 years, the burning of fossil fuels by human civilization has increased the acidity"}
{"i":127,"start_s":678.32,"end_s":680.91,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"of the ocean by 30%."}
{"i":128,"start_s":680.91,"end_s":681.13,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"So in"}
{"i":129,"start_s":681.42,"end_s":691.85,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"2007, when I was running for the U.S. Senate for the first time, the oysters started dying. And the scientists got involved. They said, \"What's"}
{"i":130,"start_s":691.85,"end_s":693.31,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"going on?\" They"}
{"i":131,"start_s":693.32,"end_s":695.76,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"said, \"Is it a virus?"}
{"i":132,"start_s":695.86,"end_s":696.47,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Is it"}
{"i":133,"start_s":696.47,"end_s":701.45,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"a bacterium?\" It wasn't a virus. It wasn't a bacterium."}
{"i":134,"start_s":701.44,"end_s":701.61,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":true,"text":"And"}
{"i":135,"start_s":701.8,"end_s":728.52,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"after some time, they nailed it down simply that the ocean water had become too acidic. Too much carbonic acid in the ocean from carbon dioxide pollution in the atmosphere. And where did that come from? From the burning of fossil fuels. So now, the water comes into the Whiskey Creek Oyster Hatchery in a very large pipe, and then it has to be buffered. That is, the acidity has to be decreased"}
{"i":136,"start_s":728.81,"end_s":731.83,"speaker":"SPEAKER_04","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"before that water continues into the vats with the baby"}
{"i":137,"start_s":731.83,"end_s":740.26,"speaker":"SPEAKER_20","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"oysters. And for all we know they'll have to do this forever more until we can turn the clock back on global"}
{"i":138,"start_s":741.32,"end_s":748.86,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"climate disruption. And if the oysters are being affected, what else is going to be affected in the sea chain? What is the impact on our coral"}
{"i":139,"start_s":749.02,"end_s":753.98,"speaker":"SPEAKER_20","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"reefs, which provide the foundation for many of the world's fisheries?"}
{"i":140,"start_s":754.25,"end_s":755.91,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Well, that's"}
{"i":141,"start_s":756.06,"end_s":757.49,"speaker":"SPEAKER_20","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"something"}
{"i":142,"start_s":757.75,"end_s":757.77,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"that"}
{"i":143,"start_s":758.15,"end_s":762.76,"speaker":"SPEAKER_20","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"we should rightly be very concerned about."}
{"i":144,"start_s":762.76,"end_s":762.94,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"So"}
{"i":145,"start_s":763.25,"end_s":771.66,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"there you have it folks, episode 3 of the Senate Climate Disruption Quiz. How did you do? How many of those questions did you get"}
